1
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:13,340
Try walking away from me and see

2
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:26,880
aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:33,980
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,260
onto the head of the carpenter
I had put in a chokehold

5
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed, saying I'm still just a brat

6
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:53,560
even if I leave some of my energy somewhere

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,620
passion or not,
a single yawn, nothing changes

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,500
the streetscape is strangely kind

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,520
from the pointed hat's water flask

10
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:16,780
toward the great hall, the sun sets

11
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:25,260
tomorrow too, how it ends, huh

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,080
Katsushika Shibamata, happy again

13
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,860
I only realized after going out everywhere,
because I'm such a fool

14
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:46,460
That day, Senpai and I were asked by his mom

15
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:49,700
to repair the crawl space
under Senpai's family home.

16
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:57,400
Are you okay, Senpai?

17
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,020
Shine the light properly!

18
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:00,620
Yes!

19
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:08,380
Just the heavy one!

20
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:08,840
Yes!

21
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,580
Senpai, what is this place?

22
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:13,540
Well...

23
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,300
It's a pot.

24
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:31,100
Looking back,
that was the start of the tragedy.

25
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:36,340
The cursed plum pickle jar.

26
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,980
Hey, pull yourself together!

27
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:09,780
The jar, the jar!

28
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:10,700
Hey!

29
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,860
The jar.

30
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:32,120
Supposedly,
my ancestor hid that jar somewhere.

31
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,920
A 400-year-old jar

32
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,820
So it really existed.

33
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:39,140
So what's inside this?

34
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:40,600
I never heard about that.

35
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:44,900
But it's a jar that a defeated samurai carried,
even at the cost of his life!

36
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:48,040
I can guess it's some kind of treasure,
at least.

37
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,140
Gold coins, or paintings...

38
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:52,549
N-n-n-n-n-n-n-n-n-n-n-n-n-n...

39
00:03:52,599 --> 00:03:56,325
Ko, ko, ko, ko, ko, ko, ko,
ko, ko, ko, ko, ko, ko, ko,

