Nngh!

153
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,280
Here we go!

154
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:31,100
Hah!

155
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:32,300
No way!

156
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,500
It's blood! No, it's not!
No, it's not! No, it's not! No, it's not!

157
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,220
Blood! Blood! Blood!

158
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,700
T-this is...

159
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:40,640
B-b-b-b-blood! It's blood!

160
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,780
Yahahahahaha! Blood! Blood!

161
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:45,920
Oh my god!

162
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:48,780
Blood! Blood! It's blood! Blood!

163
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:51,160
Seriously, look closer!
That's just a pickled plum!

164
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:54,600
A pickled plum?

165
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:57,280
So it was just a pickled plum?

166
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:58,860
Good thing it's just a pickled plum

167
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,500
But why would there be
a pickled plum in the jar?

168
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:07,220
I see, this is probably a decoy
to lull the enemy into complacency.

169
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,560
The real one is in another jar.

170
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,340
Another dummy?

171
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,900
This one too.

172
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,500
Goddamn dummies, every single one.

173
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,420
They're all pickled plums.

174
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,980
That 5 billion...

175
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:26,560
5 billion...

176
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:31,300
Senpai,
didn't a wooden box come out with them?

177
00:09:32,940 --> 00:09:35,340
Oh right,
maybe there's something valuable in that.

178
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:38,100
What, just a scrap of paper?

179
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,820
Wait, what if the jars are all decoys?

180
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:44,620
This paper must have the location
of the real treasure written on it.

181
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:45,840
I see.

182
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:53,080
Well, one day, a fallen samurai
collapsed in front of our house.

183
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:56,440
When I opened the lid of the
jar that samurai was carrying...

184
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,020
Just pickled plums?

185
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:02,480
So these are all pickled plums?

186
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:03,120
That's right.

187
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,900
Those are all jars of pickled plums.

188
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:07,500
Please, enjoy them together.

189
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:10,720
Hey, hey.

190
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:14,380
I am Adachi Shinzaemon.

191
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:19,160
I wanted to leave these pickled plums, handed down through my descendants for generations,
Translation>
but

192
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:22,080
my power was not enough,
and it came to this.

193
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:26,220
Would you please eat those in its place,
all of you?

194
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:27,520
Sure.

195
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:32,780
Really? I pickled them with great care.
I guarantee the taste.

196
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:36,280
Please eat every last one,
without leaving a single piece.

197
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:37,600
All right.

198
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:38,520
Please.

199
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:45,100
That said, I'm not fond of pickled plums.

200
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:48,340
Well, I suppose I'll bury
them along with this lot.

201
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:52,500
And so a shrine was built,
and the warrior and the jar were buried.

202
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:55,200
Anyway, five years...
grab the money, Kichi, I'm telling you.

203
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:58,380
So it really was pickled plums after all.

204
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:02,120
My attachment... my attachment...

205
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:03,400
*Slump*

206
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:06,280
So, what should we do
with these pickled plums?

207
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,740
Senpai, are you going to eat some?

208
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,860
Who could eat pickled
plums that are 400 years old?

209
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:11,940
Go throw them away somewhere.

210
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:12,720
M-me, sir?

211
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:15,560
I'm in a very bad mood right now.

212
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,660
I'll put a curse on you!

213
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:18,680
Curse you!

214
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,260
Understood!

215
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:28,760
Sorry, Mr. Adachi Shinzaemon.

216
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:32,840
Your pickled plums are being carted
off by a 20th-century garbage truck.

217
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:33,920
Don't throw them away!

218
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:40,020
You mustn't throw them away!

219
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,660
Don't throw them away!

220
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:51,560
Don't throw the jar away!

221
00:11:57,080 --> 00:12:16,900
!

222
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:18,673
I see. A movie shoot.

223
00:12:18,723 --> 00:12:22,040
Well, of course. Ghosts don't exist.

224
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:27,198
Wh-wh-

225
00:12:27,248 --> 00:12:30,860
Wh-what is this...

226
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:39,280
Don't throw the jar away!

227
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:16,880
Thank you for watching.

228
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,460
I am Adachi Shinzaemon, you know.

229
00:13:27,460 --> 00:13:31,420
You're the one who brought the jar,
aren't you?

230
00:13:31,420 --> 00:13:32,520
With mandarins...

231
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:37,880
How vexing! How vexing!

232
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:40,740
What's so vexing, Shinzaemon-san?

233
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:45,660
I pickled those plums
with all my heart and soul!

234
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:51,000
And that Ryotsu Kankichi buried them in
the ground without eating a single one!

235
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,080
So you're upset they didn't
eat the pickled plums?

236
00:13:56,780 --> 00:14:01,260
How vexing! Since it has come to this,
I'll curse you to the end of time!

237
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:05,260
By the way, who exactly will you curse?

238
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:08,280
Why, the Ryotsu family, of course!

239
00:14:10,700 --> 00:14:13,200
Good, he's completely buying it.

240
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,800
What a powerful evil spirit!

241
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:25,220
To subdue it, you'll need these talismans,
at least one or three of them!

242
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:26,140
Phew, that's a relief.

243
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,400
So I won't be cursed.

244
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:32,620
Aren't you a Ryotsu?

245
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:34,420
Yes, I'm from the Honda family.

246
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:35,520
No way!

247
00:14:43,125 --> 00:14:47,180
Since we're here, could you tell us
some easy ways to hold a memorial?

248
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:50,140
Senpai says he doesn't believe in curses,

249
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:52,200
but I thought I'd tell you just in case.

250
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:54,520
Just go eat your pickled plums.

251
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:59,660
So if an Adachi family member
eats all these pickled plums,

252
00:14:59,660 --> 00:15:03,480
the curse will supposedly vanish and the
fallen samurai's ghost won't appear anymore.

253
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:07,680
No way,
I'm not eating 400-year-old pickled plums!

254
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:09,960
But they don't seem to be rotten.

255
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,480
Pickled plums are supposed
to last a long time, right?

256
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,000
Then you eat them.

257
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,800
No way, I'm not an Adachi family member.

258
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:20,740
Just wait a moment.

259
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:29,340
Look.

260
00:15:29,340 --> 00:15:31,780
I just submitted the adoption
papers to the ward office.

261
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:34,120
From today, you're my son.

262
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,200
Hayato Ryotsu.

263
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:39,420
Now you're officially a
member of the Ryotsu family.

264
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:41,440
So this jar is

265
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:45,660
yours to handle.

266
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:48,820
You mean you want me to
eat all of them, senpai!

267
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:49,980
I'm not your senpai!

268
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,620
Call me Papa.

269
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:52,280
Papa?

270
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:53,520
Good.

271
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:56,660
No, it's not that. Dumping this
on someone so strong is just cruel!

272
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:57,120
Be quiet!

273
00:15:57,700 --> 00:16:00,540
They say a lion pushes
its cub down a deep ravine.

274
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:05,081
It's all out of love, a stern love that
wants you to grow into a strong man.

275
00:16:05,131 --> 00:16:06,020
Please understand.

276
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:07,760
N-no way, senior!

277
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,280
Call me Papa.

278
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:09,700
Papa?

279
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:12,364
If you can't eat them all,

280
00:16:12,414 --> 00:16:16,340
the curse will fall on you too,
since you're a member of the Ryotsu family.

281
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:17,700
Don't forget!

282
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:21,660
Well, that's how it is,
so take care of them!

283
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:31,440
That's awful! This is too much!
It's just too cruel!

284
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:37,180
But can we really eat these?

285
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:45,200
They don't seem to have gone bad,
but they're 400 years old, after all.

286
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,400
That time...

287
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,240
Ugh...

288
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:53,860
Aaaaaah!

289
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:57,340
Sour, but they're just ordinary umeboshi,
at least.

290
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:58,340
Mm.

291
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:00,400
Mm.

292
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:01,040
Mm.

293
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:09,040
With these, I could eat bowl after
bowl of rice with just one umeboshi.

294
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:11,540
It's good that they
make you eat more, but...

295
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:14,320
I don't need umeboshi at all!

296
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:33,360
Itadakimasu.

297
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:39,160
This sourness is irresistible!

298
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:41,040
Delicious.

299
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:48,520
So this is...

300
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:50,860
It's a reverse hinomaru bento.

301
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,220
Is this actually good?

302
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:56,500
Itadakimasu!

303
00:17:57,340 --> 00:18:02,360
Is it delicious?

304
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:03,640
It's delicious!

305
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:08,747
Today,

306
00:18:08,797 --> 00:18:12,440
Plum-flavored rice!

307
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,160
Itadakimasu!

308
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,860
Yo, Nakagawa!

309
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:25,400
What, you're actually going to eat them all?

310
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:28,380
Nobody'd notice if we tossed half of them.

311
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:29,840
I can't do that.

312
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,740
There's also the tale of Hoichi the Earless.

313
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:32,840
You can't do it half-heartedly.

314
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,600
Thank you for the meal.

315
00:18:40,800 --> 00:18:42,360
I'm stuffed.

316
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:45,900
Well, let's have some dessert.

317
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:51,680
So you're not just eating umeboshi?

318
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:53,560
Hey, give me a little too.

319
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:58,400
Water, quick!

320
00:19:01,060 --> 00:19:01,820
What is this?

321
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:06,280
It's umeboshi cake and 100% umeboshi juice.

322
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,640
If you won't eat it, Senpai, I will.

323
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:10,320
Itadakimasu.

324
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:17,980
Sweet and sour, and delicious.

325
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:46,000
I'm back.

326
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:47,520
Welcome back.

327
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:49,120
How was the trip to Kyoto?

328
00:19:49,620 --> 00:19:51,180
I managed to take it easy this time.

329
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:53,120
I brought back something rare.

330
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,140
It's probably deer crackers
or something, right?

331
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:56,120
Come on, that's not it.

332
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:58,020
I'm not giving any to a noisy guy like you.

333
00:19:58,020 --> 00:19:59,160
What is it, Chief?

334
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,080
Don't be surprised when you see it.

335
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:03,480
Well?

336
00:20:04,140 --> 00:20:06,040
Umeboshi?

337
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:08,580
That's right. I bought them at
an old established shop in Kyoto.

338
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,460
You can't be serious.

339
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,820
You can buy umeboshi in Tokyo too, you know.

340
00:20:12,820 --> 00:20:14,400
What on earth were you thinking?

341
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,600
You really don't know anything, do you?

342
00:20:17,980 --> 00:20:20,920
The longer it's aged, the deeper
the flavor and the greater the value.

343
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:24,780
By the way,
this one has been aged for 30 years,

344
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,460
and each piece costs 3,000 yen.

345
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:29,600
3,000 yen for 30 years?

346
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:30,560
So that means...

347
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,400
Pardon me for asking, Chief...

348
00:20:33,780 --> 00:20:34,280
What is it?

349
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:35,960
Hypothetically speaking,

350
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:38,800
if a 400-year-old umeboshi were found,

351
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:40,480
how much do you think it would be worth?

352
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,140
400 years old?

353
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:45,760
I doubt such a thing even exists.

354
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:48,540
But a 100-year-old one was
being sold for 10,000 yen.

355
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:51,740
One piece for 50,000 yen.
No, it might go for 100,000 yen.

356
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,940
100,000 yen per piece?

357
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:58,880
If I recall,
a jar that size holds at least 400 pieces.

358
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:02,120
So if that's 50 pieces...?

359
00:21:03,280 --> 00:21:04,060
2 billion yen?

360
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:08,920
Ryo-chan?

361
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:12,700
That son of a bitch! He's eating
something worth two billion yen?!

362
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,580
I can't just sit here!

363
00:21:15,760 --> 00:21:44,680
Waaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

364
00:21:48,360 --> 00:22:00,860
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

365
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:04,640
That was the last one! Now there's no
need to worry about the curse anymore!

366
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:06,320
What?!

367
00:22:06,540 --> 00:22:08,851
There were so many of them, though,

368
00:22:08,901 --> 00:22:12,680
don't we have even one or two left...?

369
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:14,540
None, none, not a single one!

370
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:16,920
Two billion yen!

371
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,740
Senpai...

372
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:38,000
I ate all the pickled plums!

373
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:42,940
And who are you?

374
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:47,200
For 35 years,
I've been known as the walking traffic law.

375
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:49,500
Traffic Safety Instructors Unit, Batch 7.

376
00:22:49,500 --> 00:22:50,720
Ishizuru Tetsuō.

377
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:52,280
Kenzō.

378
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:55,640
Could you be the armored
warrior that Honda saw?

379
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:56,940
Indeed.

380
00:22:56,940 --> 00:23:00,300
You were littering in public,
so I warned you.

381
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,220
But more importantly, you.

382
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:03,260
Speeding on a bicycle,

383
00:23:03,260 --> 00:23:04,460
and property damage.

384
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:06,240
That is truly unforgivable.

385
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:06,920
Therefore,

386
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:11,900
I hereby sentence you to punishment.

387
00:23:25,740 --> 00:23:29,120
When I looked up, the armored warrior
and the empty plum jar were both gone.

388
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:34,560
Maybe he came to thank us
for eating all the plums.

389
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,320
Come on, don't dawdle.

390
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:41,220
Taking out the trash at
night is strictly forbidden.

391
00:23:41,220 --> 00:23:43,580
Everything has to be
returned to its owner, got it?

392
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:47,560
Argh! Why do I have to
do this kind of thing!

393
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:50,540
On top of that, you made me pick up every last bit of my body's...
ugh, you had me carry everything!

394
00:23:50,820 --> 00:23:52,540
That's cheating, you cheat!

395
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:54,280
Yes, yes! Sorry, sorry!

396
00:23:55,240 --> 00:23:59,780
Damn it! Why is the armored
warrior's curse falling on me?!

397
00:24:04,340 --> 00:24:06,220
Nakagawa's the Shitamachi King

398
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:07,840
Hah! Don't make me laugh!

399
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:11,120
Nobody in Shitamachi hides
their front at the bathhouse!

400
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:13,280
If you've got the guts, take off that towel

401
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:15,480
Go on, try swinging it around, damn it!

402
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:18,880
Next time: Is Nakagawa a Shitamachi kid?

403
00:24:19,300 --> 00:24:21,720
Here we go, round and round and round!

404
00:24:35,980 --> 00:24:38,100
Surprise and commotion,

405
00:24:38,100 --> 00:24:38,900
Yaaah!

406
00:24:38,900 --> 00:24:43,980
Timely, tidy, t-swift,
tumbling away like a monkey.

407
00:24:43,980 --> 00:24:55,760
Timed just right, a flash of thought, bounding on,
tying it up, taking action, tumbling off.

408
00:24:56,720 --> 00:25:00,320
Above all, amazing power!

409
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:12,720
Everyone gather! Come here,
and you'll find the dreamlike final energy.

410
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:23,800
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, painting the universe,
standing on the earth, the star of Kameari spun around in a circle.

411
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:29,020
"This is good enough, right?
" "Like hell it is!"

412
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:40,880
Thank you for watching.

